# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions
/.next/
/out/
/build
/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.vercel

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment — .env holds this machine's addresses and is never shared.
# The template is committed so a fresh clone knows what to fill in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated media
#
# Everything under here is produced from `assets/` by `npm run frames` and by
# scripts/build-auth-art.mjs. Large binaries that can be rebuilt do not belong
# in a repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
public/frames
assets/frames/house/
assets/frames/camera/
assets/frames/lamp/
assets/frames/termometer/
assets/videos/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots
#
# Written by scripts/shots.mjs and scripts/app-shots.mjs during design review.
# They are review artefacts, not source, and they are large.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
shots/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
!public/**/*.png
!src/**/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assistant and design-tool working files
#
# These stay on disk — they are how a new session learns the design system and
# how to run the app — but they are not part of the published repository.
#
# launch.json is the exception: it is how the dev server is started, it is
# small, and a checkout without it cannot be run. Note the `.claude/*` form
# rather than `.claude/` — git will not re-include a file inside a directory
# it has already excluded, so the directory itself must stay walkable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json
.impeccable/
.cursor/
.aider*
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal documents
#
# README.md is the repository's own front door and stays. docs/ holds the
# design record and the product truth — working notes for building this, kept
# out of the public history but kept on disk, because the next session needs
# them to design anything consistently.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.md
!README.md
docs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.pem
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
